 "intro_html": "A rainy-day favourite: <b>whole lengths of spring onion</b> laid side by side, scattered with shrimp and squid and held together with just enough <b>ice-cold batter</b>. Plenty of oil in a well-heated steel pan makes the edges lacy and crisp. Cut into squares and dip in vinegared soy. Mild. This is a home adaptation built from several Korean sources and has not been kitchen tested.",
